-- lib-test.once: a LIBRARY (no `main`).
--
-- `swap` is polymorphic. Per D007 (Structural Type Matching), a signature is
-- an ASSERTION that structurally matches the inferred type (modulo variable
-- renaming) — so a polymorphic signature is valid; it documents the programmer's
-- understanding without changing meaning. Type variables are LOWERCASE (`a`,
-- `b`); uppercase names (`Int`, `Unit`, …) are concrete types.
--
-- A library has no `main`, so the mode is inferred as a library (no entry
-- point) and it compiles to x86_64 assembly. (The C `--lib` backend is not yet
-- implemented; native asm is the active backend.)

swap : a * b -> b * a
swap = pair snd fst
